invariant: INV-26
file: ct.h
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: the AES-GCM suite build stops needing CH_NATIVE_AES, so
  __ARM_FEATURE_AES or __AES__ alone decides that a traffic key may go to
  the AES instructions. Those macros say the instructions exist. Neither
  says their latency is independent of their operands, and the
  architectures do not promise it either, which is why Arm publishes
  FEAT_DIT and Intel publishes DOITM. ct.h refuses the same inference for
  the widening multiply and asks the build for CH_NATIVE_WIDEMUL
  (https://github.com/c4milo/chapulin/issues/53); this edit drops the
  matching rule for AES, and nothing else in the tree asks anyone to
  state the timing.

--- old
#ifndef CH_NATIVE_AES
#error "CH_SUITE_AES_GCM needs -DCH_NATIVE_AES: the build asserts the timing (quic_aes_hw.c)"
#endif
#endif
--- new
#endif
